/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * vmeInit
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * vmeInit()
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * None
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Initialize the (non-EPICS) software
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Initializes certain variables and tasks, connects interrupts to their
 * handlers, enables interrupts, calls gnirsInit() for additional
 * initialization, sets global status variables, and returns.  This
 * routine must be called once before any other calls to the VxWorks C
 * software.  It may be called more than once, but the tasks it handles
 * are done only once.  The usefully repeatable parts of the initialization
 * efforts are in gnirsInit().
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * gnirsInit
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * gnirsInit()
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * None
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Do the repeatable parts of the initialization
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * This routine may be run as often as desired.  In particular, it is
 * the one to call if the configuration files have been changed.  It
 * shuts down all the motors and mechanisms (in terms of software), then
 * initializes the hardware, verifies the hardware, and builds the various
 * software structures associated with motors and mechanisms using the
 * three configuration files.  When that is done, the digital I/O bits
 * are set according to the configuration information, the cryo head
 * switches are read/set, and finally, if all the preceeding has
 * been successful, the active motors are made available for use
 * (via initMotors()).
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * vmeBoardInit
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * vmeBoardInit()
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * None
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Initialize hardware
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Initialize the hardware associated with motors, digital I/O,
 * temperature monitoring boards and the pressure sensors.  This
 * involves both configuring data structures and setting appropriate
 * bits in the various registers associated with the VME boards.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * motorDriverInit
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * motorDriverInit()
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * None
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Set up motor driver card.
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Initializes each of the OMS motor driver cards and associated software.
 * Semaphores needed by the software are set up, input and output ring
 * buffers for communication with the OMS cards are created, and the
 * hardware is cleared.  Once that is done, the status register is
 * checked to be sure it did clear (no characters waiting to be read,
 * no characters in the transmit [to the controller] buffer, no other
 * errors).  If all is OK, interrupts are enabled, except for the
 * transmit buffer empty interrupt which is enabled only when a character
 * has been sent.
 *
 * The output ring buffer is used to hold characters waiting to be
 * transmitted to the controller card.  The sent buffer is used to record
 * what has been sent and is needed only for diagnostic purposes.
 *
 * The semOut semaphore is used to make sure that commands from multiple
 * motors are not intermixed as they are inserted into the output ring
 * buffer.  The semResponse semaphore is used to signal a task that a
 * response to a command is available.  The semDone semaphores are used
 * to signal a task that a DONE interrupt has been received: if md->waiting
 * for the axis of interest is non-zero, the appropriate semDone should
 * be given (in the interrupt routine).
 *
 * 
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * gnirsMotor0IntHndlr
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * gnirsMotor0IntHndlr(int)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) int ()
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (void) Returns 'void' and hence has no STATUS value
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Handle interrupt from OMS motor control card
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Calls motorIntHandler with (the card number) 0 as argument.  Counts
 * interrupts for diagnostic purposes only.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
